      "content_license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "body": "<h1>Undo a commit &amp; redo</h1>\n<pre class=\"lang-bash s-code-block\"><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">$ git commit -m <span class=\"hljs-string\">&quot;Something terribly misguided&quot;</span> <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># (0: Your Accident)</span>\n$ git reset HEAD~                              <span class=\"hljs-comment\"># (1)</span>\n</code></pre>\n<ol>\n<li><code>git reset</code> is the command responsible for the <strong>undo</strong>. It will undo your last commit while <em>leaving your working tree untouched</em>.</li>\n<li>Make corrections to <code>working_tree</code> files.\n<ul><li>add with <code>git add</code></li></ul></li>\n</ol>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Note:</strong> see <a href=\"/a/6866485\">this answer</a>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Alternatively:</p>\n<pre><code>git commit --amend\n</code></pre>\n"
    }
